    "body": "- `kernels.yaml`: MI300 MoE Kernels Multi-GPU, and the AITER `test_modular_kernel_combinations` run in the MI300 MoE Kernels mirror (#60322 added both to `test-amd.yaml` only).\n- `models_basic.yaml`: MI355 Kimi K3 Multi-GPU; its tests skip on the 1-GPU MI355 Kimi K3 mirror.\n- `expert_parallelism.yaml`: a gating MI355 mirror for Elastic EP Scaling, which only had a legacy MI300 job.\n- `models_distributed.yaml`, `quantization.yaml`: the 2-GPU vision test on MI300 Distributed Models shard 2, and torchao 0.18.0 for the MI300 Quantization mirror (#52183 bumped NVIDIA and `test-amd.yaml` only).\n- `test-amd.yaml`: regenerated as a copy of the test_areas AMD steps, with every step still `optional`.\n\n`test-amd.yaml` and the test_areas mirrors have drifted apart. This PR moves into test_areas only the AMD coverage that test_areas doesn't already run on some AMD GPU, so no suite gets a second AMD platform. The regenerated file drops 84 legacy groups whose tests run in test_areas under a newer label or on another AMD GPU, including the five MRV2 groups #54823 removed. It also drops the gfx950 copies of Attention, MoE and Quantization Kernels, Quantization, Language Models (PPL), CUDAGraph and V1 Spec Decode, which run on MI300 or MI250 in test_areas (#57599 kept Quantization off MI355 on purpose), and gains 68 steps main CI runs but the legacy file never had. Rendered through both ci-infra generators, all 236 AMD jobs match on queue, commands, environment, timeout and shard count; main CI gains exactly the 3 new AMD steps and only the 3 edited steps change.\n\nThe added steps are copies of legacy jobs that passed every recent `amd-ci` main nightly they ran in (MoE Kernels Multi-GPU 8/8, Kimi K3 Multi-GPU 28/28, Elastic EP on MI300 28/28). On MI355 (gfx950), Kimi K3 Multi-GPU passed 10/10 and Elastic EP 14 of 16 (the other 2 failed when another process took the GPU memory). MI300 hardware wasn't available locally. #59677 makes the torchao and MI300 MoE changes